re._flowtype = c end","after":"    local c = store._flowtype\n    -- (the generation AND the graph itself: a fresh ingest may restart the generation count)\n    if c and c.gen == store.generation and c.data == store.data and c[key] then return c[key] end\n    if not c or c.gen ~= store.generation or c.data ~= store.data then\n        c = { gen = store.generation, data = store.data }; store._flowtype = c\n    end","file":"lua/cartograph/flowtype.lua"}}},{"verb":"edit","id":"1791596162.134599-edit","invocation":{"verb":"edit","touched":["lua/cartograph/effects.lua"],"args":{"before":"require('cartograph.flowtype').of(store) or nild","after":"require('cartograph.flowtype').of(store) or nil","file":"lua/cartograph/effects.lua"}}},{"verb":"edit","id":"1791596170.308553-edit","invocation":{"verb":"edit","touched":["lua/cartograph/flowtype.lua"],"args":{"before":"local tsutil = require 'cartograph.spec.tsutil'","after":"local tsutil = require 'cartograph.spec.tsutil'\nlocal EMPTY_NODE = { child = function () return nil end } -- (an absent child list: tsutil.inext over nothing)","file":"lua/cartograph/flowtype.lua"}}},{"verb":"edit","id":"1791596356.660401-edit","invocation":{"verb":"edit","touched":[".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"],"args":{"before":"| What TYPE is this method call's receiver — `fd:close()` on a file, `n:parent()` on a tree-sitter node — and what does the call do? | The resolver's typed_receiver pass (resolve_receiver_type, CART-1570 / 1571) types a receiver from the methods called on it in one function: a member only one profile type declares, or the one type declaring every member called. Every UNRESOLVED or refused call of that receiver whose member the type declares carries `ext = { disp = 'external', why = 'typed-receiver', type = T }`. `effects` reads it as `T.member` (`file.` → io, `TSNode.` → pure, `string.` → pure). MEASURED 2026-10-10 on lua/cartograph (nvim profile active): io 198 → 267, pure 2576 → 2645, hedged summaries 4283 → 3976, no write key lost. Not yet: typing from a local's own definition (`local fd = io.open(p)`; measured: 9 joins on this repo for +4.5% extraction, dropped; it pays only on plain-Lua trees with no profile), loop element types, record fields. CART-1621 |","after":"| What TYPE is this method call's receiver — `fd:close()` on a file, `n:parent()` on a tree-sitter node — and what does the call do? | The resolver's typed_receiver pass (resolve_receiver_type, CART-1570 / 1571) types a receiver from the methods called on it in one function: a member only one profile type declares, or the one type declaring every member called. Every UNRESOLVED or refused call of that receiver whose member the type declares carries `ext = { disp = 'external', why = 'typed-receiver', type = T }`. `effects` reads it as `T.member` (`file.` → io, `TSNode.` → pure, `string.` → pure). MEASURED 2026-10-10 on lua/cartograph (nvim profile active): io 198 → 267, pure 2576 → 2645, hedged summaries 4283 → 3976, no write key lost. Not yet: typing from a local's own definition (`local fd = io.open(p)`; measured: 9 joins on this repo for +4.5% extraction, dropped; it pays only on plain-Lua trees with no profile), loop element types, record fields. CART-1621 |\n| What VALUE reaches this ambiguous call's receiver — which function `x.m()` really calls, or whether `s` is only ever a string — when the name join could only list every same-named candidate? | `require('cartograph.flowtype').of(store[, { open = false }]).verdict(call)` → `{ kind = 'exact' | 'narrowed', targets = { fn id … } }` or `{ kind = 'string' | 'typed', type }`, or nil (no claim). It is an inclusion points-to analysis (Andersen) over the Lua tree. Objects (table constructors, functions, profile TYPE objects) flow along assignments, arguments to resolved and dynamic callees, returns, `require`, `setmetatable` __index, pcall, and pairs / ipairs keys and values. Fields are per object; a dynamic-key load reads every field; the profiles' declared returns type external results and typed-method results (`s:sub` → string). `open` (the default) gives an exported function's parameters an unknown value, so no claim is made through them. A port past 64 objects drops out (opts.spread = true makes it poison its successors instead: sound, and it blanks a third of the answers). `R.stats` gives the counts. Effects use it for joined calls when `config.effects_flow` (env CARTOGRAPH_EFFECTS_FLOW=1) is on, hedged as a premise. MEASURED 2026-10-10 on lua/cartograph, 3674 ambiguous calls, open: exact 176, string 596, narrowed 2, unknown 716, none 2123; closed: exact 192 / string 780. About 25 s and +1 GB, hence opt-in. Hand-checked: 30/30 string verdicts right, and every exact disagreement with the join checked had the analysis right (at.lua's `C.sl` is bytecol's returned reader closure). Unification instead of inclusion gave 1572 wrong exacts. CART-1621 |","file":".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"}}}],"entries":[{"bytes":516,"id":"1791595659.250752-edit","decisions":[],"verb":"edit","invocation":{"verb":"edit","touched":["lua/cartograph/config.lua"],"args":{"before":"M.federated_resolve = vim.env.CARTOGRAPH_FEDERATED == '1'","after":"M.federated_resolve = vim.env.CARTOGRAPH_FEDERATED == '1'\n\n-- EFFECTS BY FLOW (CART-1621): effects ask cartograph.flowtype — an inclusion points-to analysis — what reaches an\n-- AMBIGUOUS call's receiver, before joining every same-named candidate: the one function (or the few) that flows\n-- there, or the type (`string`). The answer is a premise, hedged (~) like the join. Env CARTOGRAPH_EFFECTS_FLOW=1.\n-- Default off: the analysis is ~23 s and ~650 MB over an extraction on lua/cartograph (measured 2026-10-10)\nM.effects_flow = vim.env.CARTOGRAPH_EFFECTS_FLOW == '1'","file":"lua/cartograph/config.lua"}},"decided_by":"tactic"},{"bytes":382,"id":"1791595659.364809-edit","decisions":[],"verb":"edit","invocation":{"verb":"edit","touched":["lua/cartograph/effects.lua"],"args